## 6️⃣ Risk Management & Mitigation

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|------------|--------|------------|
| **LLM hallucination (invalid GPU code)** | Medium | CI fails, wasted hours | ‑ Enforce syntax‑check compile step before benchmarking <br>‑ Keep a “fallback” branch with manual patches |
| **Missing GPU drivers on CI runner** | Low (if using self‑hosted GPU runner) | CI cannot profile | ‑ Provide a CPU‑only fallback mode that still runs functional tests <br>‑ Document how to spin up a public GPU runner (e.g., GitHub Actions “ubuntu‑latest‑gpu”) |
| **Large codebase → slow static analysis** | Medium | Long CI times | ‑ Cache the SQLite metadata between runs (GitHub Action cache) <br>‑ Limit analysis to files that changed (`git diff`) |
| **Security of API keys** | Low | Credential leak | ‑ Store LLM keys in GitHub Secrets, never in repo <br>‑ Rotate every month |
| **Vendor lock‑in (only AMD)** | Low | Limits portability | ‑ Design the benchmark wrapper to accept `rocprof` **or** `nvprof` via config flag |

